  "raw_text": "Step 1: Calculate the circumference of the unicycle's wheel.\nThe formula for the circumference \\(C\\) of a circle is \\(C = 2\\pi r\\), where \\(r\\) is the radius.\nGiven that the radius \\(r = 9\\) inches, we have \\(C = 2\\pi \\times 9 = 18\\pi\\) inches.\n\nStep 2: Determine the distance traveled by the unicycle in 3 seconds.\nSince the wheel makes 2 revolutions in 3 seconds, the distance traveled in 3 seconds is \\(2 \\times 18\\pi = 36\\pi\\) inches.\n\nStep 3: Calculate the speed of the unicycle in inches per second.\nSpeed is the distance traveled divided by the time taken. Here, the distance is \\(36\\pi\\) inches and the time is 3 seconds.\nSo, the speed \\(v\\) is given by \\(v = \\frac{36\\pi}{3} = 12\\pi\\) inches per second.\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{12\\pi}<|im_end|>",
